course: dictionary
lesson: 16135
title: Whizz and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their job in a sentence. Whizz can be a doing word, a naming word, or part of a phrase. «The bike whizzed down the hill.» Here whizz is something moving very fast. Ask yourself what is happening: a bike is moving quickly, so whizz means to move fast.
explain: «Mia is a maths whizz; she finished the test first.» Now a whizz is a person who is very good at something. The clues are maths and finished first. This use is informal, so you will hear it in everyday talk more than in formal writing.
explain: «We whizzed through our spellings in five minutes.» To whizz through something means to do it very quickly. Swap in fast or quickly and the sentence still makes sense. That check helps you know you have the right meaning.
fact: Whizz is a verb: to whizz, it whizzes, it whizzed, it is whizzing.
fact: Whizz is also a noun: a whizz at maths is someone who is very skilled at maths.
fact: «Whizz» means to move very fast, often with a buzzing or whistling sound.
fact: «Whizz through» means to do something very quickly, as in «whizz through the homework».
fact: Whiz is another spelling, used mainly in American English. Both spellings are correct and mean the same thing.
exercise: «The arrow whizzed past the target.» What does whizzed mean? | Fell softly to the ground | Changed colour | Was painted red | *Moved very fast
exercise: Ella says, «Sam is a computer whizz.» What does whizz mean here? | A machine that makes a loud noise | Someone who is always late | *Someone who is very good at computers | A slow, careful walker
exercise: «We whizzed through the reading book.» Which word could replace whizzed through without changing the meaning? | *raced through | went under | gave up | slept through
test: «The cars whizzed by the school gate.» What does whizzed by mean? | Stopped for a rest | Waited for the bell | Turned around and came back | *Went past very fast
test: «Our class has a few whizz-kids who love puzzles.» What is a whizz-kid? | A child who never does homework | A child who falls asleep in class | *A child who is very skilled at something | A child who runs very slowly
exam: Which sentence uses whizz as a noun? | The train will whizz past soon | He whizzed down the slide | They whizzed around the park | *She is a whizz at spelling
